    "OverallSummary": "This case involves Signet Securities' willful violation of Regulation Best Interest (Reg BI) Care Obligation from June 30, 2020, through the present. The firm recommended and sold 13 Regulation D private placement offerings totaling $140 million to investors, including accredited retail investors. The Care Obligation violation occurred because Signet's due diligence process was insufficient - it was limited to documents provided by the issuer (Company A) without independent verification or investigation. The analytical steps to identify this violation included: 1) Determining that the firm recommended private placements to retail investors; 2) Examining the firm's due diligence process; 3) Concluding that the due diligence was inadequate under Reg BI standards which require independently verifying issuer claims; and 4) Assessing that the firm lacked a reasonable basis to believe these recommendations could be in the best interest of retail investors. Additionally, the firm had supervisory failures related to outside business activities of representatives who were also employed by an affiliate of Company A, creating potential conflicts of interest. The firm also failed to deliver Form CRS to 282 retail customers between June 30, 2020, and April 14, 2022, and subsequently failed to deliver it to existing customers. These violations resulted in a $100,000 fine, censure, and undertaking to remediate issues."
